        'en' => [
            'title'   => 'Laser engraving tumblers: how to choose a rotary attachment',
            'slug'    => 'laser-engraving-tumblers-rotary-attachment',
            'excerpt' => 'Laser engraving tumblers, mugs and rings needs a rotary attachment – find out which one fits your xTool and which laser suits steel, glass or wood.',
            'blocks'  => [
                [ 'p', 'Laser engraving tumblers, mugs, bottles and rings requires a rotary attachment that turns the item under the beam. xTool offers two: the RA3 for the P3, X1, M2 (as the RA3 Lite) and the F series, and the RA2 Pro for the S1, F2, F2 Ultra UV and F1 Ultra. You choose the laser by surface: a diode or CO₂ laser for powder-coated tumblers and wood, MOPA or IR for bare steel, UV for glass.' ],
                [ 'p', 'Below we explain the difference between roller and chuck mode, what the xTool data says about the RA3 and RA2 Pro, which rotary fits which machine and how to set up a tumbler, wine glass or wedding band so the first piece doesn’t end up in the bin.' ],
                [ 'h2', 'How does a rotary attachment for a laser engraver work: rollers or chuck?' ],
                [ 'p', 'A laser engraves on a flat plane, but a tumbler is a cylinder. Instead of moving the head along one axis, a rotary attachment turns the item: the laser burns a line along the tumbler, the rotary turns it by a small angle, and so on until the design wraps around the wall. With galvo lasers such as the F series, the software usually splits the design into narrow strips and rotates the item between them. For the dimensions to come out right, the software needs the item’s diameter.' ],
                [ 'h3', 'Roller mode: quick for straight cylinders' ],
                [ 'p', 'The item rests on rollers, some of which are driven and turn it by friction. Setup is quick and item length is limited only by the machine, which makes this the most convenient mode for straight tumblers, bottles, glasses and mugs without a handle. The weak points: a light or slippery item slips, a handle catches on the frame, and a tapered item creeps sideways as it turns.' ],
                [ 'h3', 'Chuck mode: a secure grip for awkward shapes' ],
                [ 'p', 'Jaws similar to a lathe chuck grip the item by its rim, from the inside or the outside, and the motor turns it directly; the other end usually rests on a support. There is no slipping, and the chuck can hold a mug with a handle, a stemmed glass or a tapered item. The trade-off is a longer setup and the risk that jaws tightened too hard scratch a soft item.' ],
                [ 'h3', 'What the xTool data says about the RA3 and RA2 Pro' ],
                [ 'p', 'The RA3 combines four modes: roller, chuck, sphere and ring. Magnetic MagSwap™ parts make assembly and mode changes quick, and according to xTool the mode is recognised automatically. New features include batch processing in roller and chuck mode, one-step angle adjustment for engraving the inside of a ring and an enlarged 130 mm chuck for bigger items. With the P3, you also get an accurate 3D preview and autofocus based on 360° LiDAR mapping.' ],
                [ 'p', 'The RA3 comes as the RA3 Lite for the M2 and as the RA3 for the X1, P3 and F series, while a Chuck Kit and a Roller Extension Kit are listed as separate variants. Before ordering, check which variant matches your machine – we’re happy to help you choose.' ],
                [ 'p', 'The RA2 Pro is a 4-in-1 rotary with the same four modes; don’t confuse it with the older RA2, which according to xTool only has roller mode. The accessory kit for the RA2 Pro expands the range of items you can process, helps with focus alignment and works with various table tops. The RA2 Pro Plus bundle combines the rotary with this kit.' ],
                [ 'products', '9089336017109,8309744009429,8233870033109' ],
                [ 'h2', 'Which rotary attachment fits which xTool laser?' ],
                [ 'p', 'The choice of rotary depends first and foremost on your machine. The table is based on xTool’s compatibility data.' ],
                [ 'table', [ 'Machine', 'Laser', 'Rotary', 'Notes' ], [
                    [ 'xTool P3', 'CO₂, 80 W', 'RA3', '3D preview and LiDAR autofocus with the RA3' ],
